From a4fcf87fbd74b1dbf000e1c494660e267d442ba1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Z.ai Compiler Engineering" <zai@localhost>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:05:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] stack_layout: gate tier-3 slot reuse to canonical size
 classes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tier-3 block-local coalescer buckets every freed slot that is not
16/8 bytes into the 4-byte free list, and allocation selected from the
list for ANY small size — including 12-byte va_arg temps. A 12-byte
value reusing a 4-byte slot (a) wrote 12 bytes over the two live slots
following that offset and (b) left block_peak unchanged, so total_space
undercounted and the deepest slot landed below the emitted subl
frame — inside the prologue's push-staging area, where push %esi/%edi
clobbered it at runtime.

Manifestation: stdarg-3.c (i686, all levels) wrote the va_arg struct to
fini_array instead of the global (s2 read back as 0 while the sibling
in-frame y worked); pr78170.c (-O0) aborted on the same class. qemu+gdb
remote debugging pinned edi=0x0804b004 vs &s2=0x0804b104 with eax
correct — the home-slot round-trip lost the store to the push zone.

Fix: reuse is now allowed only for the canonical classes 4/8/16/32; the
release side keeps bucketing wider frees into free_4 (a narrower value
reusing a wider ex-slot is sound). Non-canonical sizes always allocate
fresh, so block_peak grows by the exact size and the frame accounting
stays closed.

i686 targeted A/B (1032 cases x O0/O1/O2): 5 sources fixed (stdarg-3,
pr78170, 20050121-1, 20070614-1, medce-1), NEW 0, CHANGED 0. Unit
1319/0; regression suite 509/0/AB-diff 0.
---
 src/backend/stack_layout/slot_assignment.rs | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/stack_layout/slot_assignment.rs b/src/backend/stack_layout/slot_assignment.rs
index d3e56508..950facc4 100644
--- a/src/backend/stack_layout/slot_assignment.rs
+++ b/src/backend/stack_layout/slot_assignment.rs
@@ -936,7 +936,20 @@ pub(super) fn assign_tier3_block_local_slots(
             // into a slot previously owned by an 8-byte value would leave that
             // value's stale upper half readable by later 64-bit accesses.
             // Protected values (DynAlloca results, vector temps) must get unique slots.
-            let can_reuse = !state.protected_slot_values.contains(&dest_id);
+            //
+            // Reuse is additionally gated to the four canonical size classes.
+            // The release side buckets EVERY non-16/8 size into free_4, so a
+            // 12-byte value used to reuse a 4-byte slot: its 12-byte extent
+            // then overlapped the two slots following that offset (silent
+            // corruption of live neighbours) AND block_peak never grew, so
+            // total_space undercounted and the deepest slot landed below the
+            // emitted `subl $N` frame — where the prologue's push-staging
+            // (push %esi/%edi) clobbers it (stdarg-3 va_arg temp: s2 written
+            // to fini_array instead of the global). Non-canonical sizes are
+            // never freed into a list they can safely share: allocate fresh
+            // (block_peak grows by the exact size — accounting stays sound).
+            let can_reuse = !state.protected_slot_values.contains(&dest_id)
+                && matches!(slot_size, 4 | 8 | 16 | 32);
             let free_list = if slot_size >= 32 {
                 &mut free_32
             } else if slot_size == 16 {
