From 5a908c0498b33e28b99d0c7d1f57f4be5d9cdd15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Z.ai Compiler Engineering" <zai@localhost>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:31:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] builtins: implement __builtin_shuffle (GCC vector
 extension)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

__builtin_shuffle(v, mask) | __builtin_shuffle(v1, v2, mask):
result[i] = concat(v1, v2)[mask[i] mod N], mask elements unsigned.
Fully unrolled runtime-indexed gather — correct for constant AND
variable masks, any element width, any lane count; pow2 lane counts
lower the index reduction to AND. The mask element count is type-checked
against the vector (GCC requires equality).

Return convention matches lower_vector_assign / rhs_is_small_vector_call
exactly: <=8-byte vectors travel as packed register values (Load of
packed_store_type(total)); >8-byte vectors by memory (the result alloca
pointer). Getting this wrong stored the alloca ADDRESS into the
destination on amd64 (si={ptr_lo,ptr_hi}).

Fixes gcc.c-torture pr85331 (V2DF reverse) and pr94591 (V2SI/V2DI
identity through vector-type casts) at O0/O1/O2 on BOTH backends —
previously undefined-symbol failures (implicit __builtin_shuffle).

Pin: tests/regression/builtin_shuffle_convention.c. Unit 1319/0;
regression suite 510/0/AB-diff 0.
